---
description: Rube Goldberg Hello World project rules for Cursor
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `.kilo/operating.md` at the repository root before making
changes and follow them.

- Milestone-driven development: one milestone at a time per
  `docs/architecture.md` section 29; track scope and acceptance in
  `docs/implementation-status.md`.
- Required gates (must all pass): `make prerequisites`, `make format`, `make
  lint`, `make unit`, `make coverage`, `make build`. Use `STRICT=1` to fail on
  missing toolchains; run integration/e2e gates when the change requires them.
- Non-negotiable integrity rules: only the CLI, orchestrator, and glyph
  catalog may see the requested plaintext; downstream events must never
  contain `targetText`, `expectedCharacter`, `unicodeCodePoint`, or
  equivalent fields (`docs/architecture.md` section 7).
- Pin all dependency and container versions; never use `latest` tags.
- Do not combine service languages; do not bypass required protocols
  (REST, SOAP, gRPC, Kafka, SSE).
- Complete required PR verification before opening the PR; never defer visual,
  integration, or e2e checks to after merge.
- Parallelize only across disjoint ownership boundaries or isolated worktrees;
  run final gates serially and keep long-lived processes in the background.
- For user-visible UI changes, verify fresh viewport captures (phone/laptop at
  minimum; responsive changes also cover relevant tablet/desktop/wide widths)
  plus the changed browser interactions.
- Do not add explanatory comments; write idiomatic code and keep it
  readable.
- Never commit unless explicitly authorized.
